Five: Watch Puzzle Games — Privacy Policy
Last updated: October 29, 2026

The short version: Five does not collect, transmit, or sell any of your data.
The games run entirely on your Apple Watch.

DEVELOPER
Five is developed by Dzianis Milasheuski, an individual developer based in
Lithuania. Questions about this policy: info@porconova.com

WHAT WE COLLECT
Nothing. Five has no analytics, no ads, no tracking, no accounts, and no
servers that receive your data. There is no sign-up and no login. We do not
know who you are, which games you play, or how you play them.

HOW THE APP WORKS
- Puzzles are generated on the watch itself from a puzzle number and a
  difficulty. Nothing is downloaded to create them and nothing is uploaded.
- To let you continue where you left off, the app stores on the watch, in its
  own private storage: the current board of each game (including Undo steps),
  the number of puzzles you have solved per difficulty, your 2048 best score
  and highest tile, and which game you chose as your free game.
- It also stores a few settings: whether haptics are on, the game you played
  last (for the Resume card), whether you have seen the welcome screens, and
  whether Full Version is unlocked as last confirmed by the App Store, so that
  games you own do not appear locked for a moment at launch.
- These files and settings never leave the watch through the app. Like other
  app data, they may be included in the backup of your Apple Watch that Apple
  keeps on your paired iPhone; that backup is handled by Apple, not by us.
- The watch-face complication only opens the app. It shows a fixed symbol and
  reads none of your data.
- The app does not use the network for gameplay, and it does not use the
  camera, the microphone, your location, your health data, your contacts, or
  your photos. It does not read any device or advertising identifier.

WHAT LEAVES YOUR DEVICE
Nothing is sent to us, ever. The only communication the app starts is with
Apple's App Store, to show the price of Full Version, to make a purchase you
confirm, and to check or restore that purchase (see PURCHASES).

PURCHASES
One game of your choice is free forever. Full Version, which unlocks all five
games, is a one-time, non-recurring In-App Purchase sold through Apple's App
Store. Apple, not the developer, processes payment and handles your Apple
Account. We receive no personal or payment information — only whether this
Apple Account holds a valid Full Version entitlement, which the app checks with
Apple on the watch using StoreKit. Restore Purchases asks Apple to sync your
purchases; Apple may ask you to sign in. Family Sharing is supported: if a
family organiser shares Full Version, Apple tells the app that the entitlement
is valid, and nothing about your family group is shared with us.

YOUR RIGHTS
Because the app collects no personal information on the developer's side,
there is no developer-held data for you to access, correct, export, or delete.
- Data stored on the watch can be removed by deleting the app, or inside it:
  Settings → Reset Progress clears every board, solved count and record.
  Your free-game choice stays, because it is part of what you are entitled to.
- No data about you is held anywhere else.

CHILDREN
Five is a set of logic puzzles suitable for all ages. It collects no data from
anyone, including children under the age of 13, and contains no ads, no links
out of the app, and no social features.

REGULATORY NOTES
The app is designed so that no directly identifying personal information
(name, email, IP address, advertising identifier, account ID) is collected by
the developer or by any third party the developer uses. The app contains no
third-party SDKs. Its privacy manifest declares no tracking, no tracking
domains and no collected data types; the only required-reason API it uses is
on-device storage of its own settings (UserDefaults, reason CA92.1). In App
Store terms, the app's privacy label is "Data Not Collected".

CHANGES
If this policy changes, the new version will be published at the same address
with a new date at the top.

